WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:01.468
And OUTFRONT now, Putin's

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.502
former speechwriter.

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.037
Abbas Gallyamov.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:04.471
And Abbas,

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.406
thank you so much for your time.

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.307
We're hearing

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:08.942
about these heavy losses

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:12.112
for the Russian army You know Putin well.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:14.280
You have been watching him closely.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.751
What do you see right now?

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:21.054
Well, I see that

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:24.391
he is in a kind of a loss.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.126
Judging by his actions,

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:26.493
you know,

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:27.560
like physically, who

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.930
he seems to be in good shape, much better

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:34.768
than he was in in spring and say,

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.136
April and May.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.371
But judging by his actions

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.274
is making mistakes here.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.575
He's acting erratically.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.376
You know,

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.347
a lot of things which seem to be illogic

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.415
like he's appointing

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:50.283
one person, promoting one person.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.251
Then in a couple of months,

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.852
he is demoting him.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.888
He's giving too much power to precautions

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.689
and taking power from precaution

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:57.724
against the same.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:58.491
Was Medvedev

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.193
the same with the prime minister?

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:03.930
So it's a kind of like if it looks like,

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:07.167
you know, as if he is at a loss

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.736
He understands that he has to act,

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.871
but he doesn't know what to me.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.207
So his hands are moving by themselves

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.308
and he's just

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.577
lifting balances and counterbalances

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:18.845
and creating new balances.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.747
And you better balance

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.450
with the things he was doing.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.685
For many years he's accustomed to doing.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:28.054
But now this is a different situation.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:28.955
He needs a

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:30.890
different kind of action,

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.426
but he's unable to deliver that.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.528
Now, in this context,

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:36.763
here of watching Putin,

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.765
I know you're focused on the next Russian

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:40.667
presidential election

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.202
and you believe that Putin needs

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:44.003
to announce his candidacy

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.271
in the coming months.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.473
So if he's going to run,

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.608
he needs to announce that

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:49.943
in the coming months.

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.711
But you think he may cancel

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.713
the elections? What would that mean?

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.484
Well, judging

00:01:57.484 --> 00:02:00.620
by his actions, when he is escalating

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.356
constantly without necessity,

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.059
he might really cancel the elections.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:09.629
Uh, understanding that he will

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.298
without victory over Ukraine,

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.668
he will face a reality difficulties

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:16.970
with getting

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.438
the majority of votes of Russians,

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:19.038
you know,

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.174
without proving that he's strong Russian.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.009
The Russians would need him

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.711
if he is not strong.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:27.747
So he might really declare

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:30.817
the martial law and cancel the elections.

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.086
You know, people will be facing

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.454
more and more difficulties

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:37.624
The Russian economy is deteriorating.

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.192
The war.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.461
The war is is lost.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.829
But there are more and more dead

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.397
bodies coming

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:45.932
to Russia.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.667
Russians will be

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.003
coming across more and more difficulties

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.304
in their daily lives,

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.539
and they'll be

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:55.175
trying to find the explanation

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.343
why this is happening to us.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.712
And in this situation,

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.548
they're looking around in politics

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:02.615
into the political process,

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.350
and they'll be answering themselves.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:04.617
Well,

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.685
this is because our country

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.720
is governed by a no parent

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.389
and no dictator.

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:12.692
And and at this moment, I think

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.861
a military force

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.763
or an elite or broadly

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.598
speaking, will become possible.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.333
So in one year,

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.402
when the political situation changes

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.304
and there is a really hated,

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.772
unpopular president

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.773
at the head of the country,

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.841
and the war is real unpopular,

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.777
and they need to shed blood

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:34.080
for this Well, at this moment,

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:36.583
it all becomes a real possibility.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.518
And just to be clear,

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.485
you're saying

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.588
this is a possible military coup

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.591
Well, I can say

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:47.293
military, but it's also possible to say

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.329
they will definitely have some

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:52.198
civilian allies to broaden this speaking.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.600
It would be like

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.402
military elite or something in between.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.105
All right, Abbas, thank you very much.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:01.207
I appreciate your time.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.909
Thank you very much.

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.611
And now I want to go OUTFRONT

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:05.311
to the former U.S.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.380
ambassador to Russia, John Sullivan.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.014
And, Ambassador,

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:09.382
it's good to see you again.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.116
You hear a boss

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.251
talking about a change

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.518
that he's seen in Putin's behavior

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:14.087
since the beginning of the war.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.488
Concurring with you

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:15.822
that he

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.724
thinks he looks physically well right

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:19.626
now, but referring to him as erratic

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:21.861
and it looks as if he is at a loss

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.696
in terms of what to do.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:24.764
What do you see right now

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.232
and have you seen such a shift?

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:28.768
Well, thanks, Aaron.

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:30.103
It's good to be with you again.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:30.503
Well, I'd

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:31.971
say I'd attribute it

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:35.074
to the stress of being one year

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:39.545
into a failed massive war that he started

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:43.416
He's flailing for ways to try to address

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:45.418
the obvious

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.487
shortcomings of his special

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.222
military operation

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:51.124
and he's operating under a lot of stress.

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:52.125
I think that accounted

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:54.060
for the change we saw

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.763
in his physical appearance last year.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.433
He is in a very, very difficult spot.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.169
And I think that's reflected in

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:05.204
his actions and his decisions.

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:07.573
And he doesn't have many go up.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:08.007
No.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.375
And, you know, in this

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:10.877
actually context, it's interesting

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:13.646
because you were the last person.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.181
You spent a lot of time with him.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.583
You know what you're talking about here,

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.052
your new replacement, the new U.S.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.119
ambassador to Russia, actually

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.454
arrived in Moscow today. Right.

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:22.889
It was just today.

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:23.723
And Ambassador,

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:24.924
there were a group of protesters

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:25.825
there to greet her

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:26.459
and they were chanting,

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:27.794
war is a business for the US.

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:28.494
And, of course,

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:28.728
I guess

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:29.562
just to state the obvious

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:30.396
to everyone watching,

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:33.032
Russia does not have, you know, protests

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.367
except for when it does

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:34.701
as it

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:35.468
except for when

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:37.637
it's officially sanctioned.

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:39.405
And what do you make of this today?

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.507
Well, anyone

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:41.874
who was

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.142
protesting outside

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.078
the Russian foreign ministry

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:46.579
without the authorization

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:47.914
of the Russian government

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:49.115
would not only been

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.317
taken away immediately by the police,

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:53.920
but prosecuted and sent to prison.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.322
This protest is obviously organized

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:57.790
by the Russian government.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.292
They organized protests

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:01.060
outside our embassy

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.762
when I was ambassador.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:03.629
Usually they were

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:05.498
for a short period of time.

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:07.467
We suspected that the people were paid

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:09.402
for their time. Maybe an hour.

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:10.803
They bring video cameras

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.071
that videotape

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:14.207
people with signs, chanting slogans,

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:15.675
and then they'd go home.

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:16.476
I'm confident

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:18.144
this is what happened to my

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:20.380
successor, Ambassador Tracy.

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:23.950
So to

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:26.986
win is a very,

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:28.588
very accomplished diplomat.

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:29.522
I mean, she's

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:30.423
used to dealing

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:33.059
with this type of situation.

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:35.027
But I must say, in three years

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:36.062
as ambassador,

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.897
I never had that happen to me.

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:41.567
I had crowds outside the MFA, media

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:44.704
cameras, video cameras, but

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:46.839
I never had protesters with signs

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:49.075
when I was going into the MFA.

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:50.643
And I think this is just a sign

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:52.078
of how

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:53.913
badly fractured our relationship

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:55.948
now is with Russia.

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:57.116
Well, today, the former U.K.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:57.683
prime minister

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:58.785
Boris Johnson, talked

00:06:58.785 --> 00:07:01.254
about a conversation he had with Putin.

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:02.822
And this was literally

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:04.524
just ahead of the invasion.

00:07:04.524 --> 00:07:06.125
And when you talk about fractured

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:07.727
relationships, here's what Boris

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:08.428
Johnson said.

00:07:08.428 --> 00:07:09.695
Putin said to him, listen to this.

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:12.165
You know, he he

00:07:12.165 --> 00:07:12.932
sort of he threatened me

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:15.001
at one point and said, you know,

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:17.203
Boris, I don't want to hurt you, but

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:17.804
with a missile,

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:18.671
it would only take a minute

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:19.238
or something like that.

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:19.672
You know,

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:23.142
you know, Johnny

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:25.511
Ambassador, the Kremlin

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:27.480
spokesperson, Dmitry Peskov, said today

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.848
in response to that, what Mr.

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:30.783
Johnson said is not true.

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:33.753
More precisely, it is a lie.

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:35.621
What do you make of this?

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:38.791
Oh, I'm confident that

00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:40.560
the former prime minister is speaking

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.294
the truth.

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:42.328
I saw it myself

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:43.262
when I would engage

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:45.498
with senior Russian leaders.

00:07:45.498 --> 00:07:48.401
The conversation would go from zero

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:50.069
to 60 miles an hour

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:53.673
from a discussion about arcane aspects of

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.108
the Minsk agreements on trying to settle

00:07:56.309 --> 00:07:57.777
the Ukraine problem

00:07:57.777 --> 00:07:59.111
to a nuclear standoff

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:01.347
between the United States and Russia.

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:02.615
And I'd be taken aback

00:08:02.615 --> 00:08:04.650
when my Russian interlocutor

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.286
would start talking about nuclear war.

00:08:07.687 --> 00:08:08.521
My reaction to

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:11.290
that was if I had raised on my own

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:14.694
nuclear war I might.

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:15.394
The president

00:08:15.394 --> 00:08:15.995
I worked for,

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:17.396
President Biden would,

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:19.465
if we called me, fired me,

00:08:19.465 --> 00:08:21.501
and probably set me to have my head

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:22.468
examined.

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:24.871
What a negotiate tactic by the Russians.

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:27.106
It's one they've used all the time.

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:29.108
And I'm confident that

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:31.244
the President Putin

00:08:31.244 --> 00:08:33.112
would say something like that.

00:08:33.112 --> 00:08:36.215
Ambassador Sullivan, thank you very much.

00:08:36.215 --> 00:08:36.849
Thank you very.

